-------------------------------------------------------------------------
FINDINGS (backlog — NOT the basis of this FAIL)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
F1 (criterion 3 / D-SY-f, spec-silent): the excluded-group `Total` accumulates
   `math.Abs(t.Amount)` per row, so a refund inside a flagged group INFLATES
   the displayed group total, while the living-expense side accumulates the
   SIGNED amount so refunds REDUCE it. The two figures therefore use opposite
   refund conventions, and the "excluded" amount shown to the user will not
   equal the amount actually removed from living expenses whenever a refund is
   present. The spec pins neither convention for ExcludedGroups (D-SY-e says
   only "accumulated at the sync site from actually-skipped rows"), so I do
   not fail on it — but it is the rendered-arithmetic class (ruling
   2026-08-29b) and the major-expenses page already uses net-spend elsewhere.
   Worth a lead ruling before SY4 makes a second surface render this figure.
F2 (deferred by design, D-SY-g): living ACTUALS still include flagged spend
   while the synced TARGET now excludes it. Documented gap owned by SY4.
   Confirmed in scope-terms only: no metrics/dashboard file was touched.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------
SUMMARY
-------------------------------------------------------------------------
Criteria 1, 2, 4, 5, 6: PASS, each on a command whose output is quoted above,
with the load-bearing tests proven by mutation rather than by inspection.
Criterion 3: FAIL on D-SY-d's explicit "slice order must be deterministic"
requirement — two flagged defs sharing a Name produce 2 distinct
syncPlanHash values over 40 runs on unchanged data, which is exactly the
preview/apply hash break the decision forbids; and the test named for that
guarantee survives deletion of the sort it guards.
If the lead rules the duplicate-Name case out of SY1's scope, every other
criterion is independently satisfied and the task passes as built.
